/-!
# B-line axis program (`AxisU6`), part 3: the slab passes as `PassOK` steps

The slab passes (B1, `J6SegILSlab8`) read the skeleton registers
`rC = flatC cs`, `rM = [2 post]`, `rNC = [|cs|]`, `rNB = [pre]`, `rTOT = [pre · n' · 2 post]`
(and `rK1 = [2^(P-p)]`, `rK2 = [2^p]` for the output pass). They are built from the descriptor
by a set-up / tear-down pair:

* `SetupS Isym tbl stUp stDn ρ dA desc V C`: from any managed state in which only `0`, `sZ`,
  `dA` and the registers `ρ` may be nonempty (registers empty, `desc` on `dA`), `stUp` writes the
  register file `V` and `stDn` clears it, everything else unchanged, each at cost `≤ C`
  (B1's source-table producers and `ctlB`; `J6SegILSrc*`, `J6SegILCtl*`).
* `slabV cs pre post n' K1 K2`: the register file on `ρS = (rC, rM, rNC, rNB, rTOT, rK1, rK2)`.

`slabId_ok`, `slabSc_ok` (`PassOK`) and `slabOut_ok` (`Pass2OK`): set-up; the B1 pass; tear-down.
-/

